1
00:00:04,200 --> 00:00:08,264
This program is intended for authorized F.A.L.C.O.N. personnel only.

2
00:00:08,964 --> 00:00:13,111
If you are not authorized personnel, please stop the tape now.

3
00:00:14,711 --> 00:00:15,424
Thank you.

4
00:00:19,724 --> 00:00:24,941
The Federal Agency for Liminal Classification & Occult Nature presents

5
00:00:26,741 --> 00:00:28,515
WATER SAFETY AND YOU

6
00:00:31,115 --> 00:00:34,325
Congratulations on your assignment to the poolrooms.

7
00:00:35,125 --> 00:00:36,641
The lights are always on.

8
00:00:37,141 --> 00:00:38,895
Except where they are not.

9
00:00:41,295 --> 00:00:42,726
You are not alone here.

10
00:00:46,026 --> 00:00:46,971
This is The Wader.

11
00:00:47,571 --> 00:00:50,444
It has no eyes. It does not need them.

12
00:00:52,144 --> 00:00:58,300
The Wader hunts by sound alone. Any disturbance of the water is heard almost instantly.

13
00:00:58,800 --> 00:01:01,554
Wade slowly. Keep your hands still.

14
00:01:03,454 --> 00:01:06,912
It cannot leave the water. Dry ground is safe.

15
00:01:08,812 --> 00:01:15,568
The higher the fall, the louder the splash. The Wader will almost always hear it, and it will charge.

16
00:01:16,768 --> 00:01:19,610
It is faster than you. Get out of the water.

17
00:01:21,510 --> 00:01:24,779
If you cannot reach dry ground, stop moving.

18
00:01:25,279 --> 00:01:27,649
It will search for you by feel.

19
00:01:30,849 --> 00:01:35,786
Personnel who remain perfectly still survive the search seventy percent of the time.

20
00:01:37,786 --> 00:01:39,401
Remain perfectly still.

21
00:01:42,301 --> 00:01:43,880
Listen for its clicking.

22
00:01:44,280 --> 00:01:47,897
Steady clicking means it is hunting a sound. Freeze.

23
00:01:51,097 --> 00:01:55,124
If the clicking becomes a screech, it is charging. Move.

24
00:02:00,524 --> 00:02:04,301
If a member of your team is taken, do not attempt a rescue.

25
00:02:05,201 --> 00:02:11,239
The Wader will feed for six to ten seconds. During this time, it ignores all sound.

26
00:02:12,139 --> 00:02:13,182
Use this time.

27
00:02:15,382 --> 00:02:17,883
Taken personnel sometimes come back.

28
00:02:18,883 --> 00:02:20,735
Do not ask them about the water.

29
00:02:23,435 --> 00:02:24,060
Remember.

30
00:02:24,560 --> 00:02:25,474
Stay dry.

31
00:02:26,074 --> 00:02:27,042
Stay quiet.

32
00:02:27,642 --> 00:02:28,572
Stay still.

33
00:02:29,472 --> 00:02:30,707
And above all.

34
00:02:31,257 --> 00:02:32,357
Do not fall in.

35
00:02:35,057 --> 00:02:39,242
This concludes your orientation. Thank you for your service.

36
00:02:48,642 --> 00:02:52,898
It can hear yours.

